To deploy a complete application

1. Create a new service
	>> sudo docker service create --mode global -p 8003:80 --name Apache2 httpd
2. To check if the containers are running
	>> sudo docker ps
3. To check service details
	>> sudo docker service ps Apache2
4. To check if it works
	>> curl http://172.31.44.254:8003
5. To connect to more than one clusters  have to create overlay network
	>> sudo docker network create -d overlay myoverlay
		-- overlay is the default name
6. To check if the network is registered
	>> sudo docker network ls
7. Deploy the first service 
	a. Create the service named webapp1
		>> sudo docker service create --name webapp1 --network myoverlay -p 8001:80 hshar/webapp
	b. Check if the service is created 
		>> sudo docker service ls
8. Deploy the second service mysql
	a. Create the service
		>> sudo docker service create --name mysql --network myoverlay -p 3306:3306 hshar/mysql:5.5
9. To go inside the container 
	>> sudo docker exec -it containerid bash 
		-it is interactive
		container id is the id of the sql service 
	>> bash command line displays like sql prompt

	a. To go to mysql prompt
		>> mysql -u root -p //password is edureka
	b. Work inside sql, show database
		>> show databases;
	c. Create database
		>> create database dockerdb;
	d. Use database;
		>> use dockerdb;
	e. To list out the tables
		>> show tables;


		
